Final Reflection
Yes, my prompt improved a lot. Version 1 gave a short, vague plan, and Version 4 gave a plan I could really use. The biggest changes were adding context, listing exactly what I wanted, and asking for tables.
Overall Reflection
What makes a prompt effective? It is clear and specific. It says the task, the context, who it is for, and the format.
Most useful technique: Role prompting with an audience and format, because it changed a plain answer into one I could use. Improving the prompt step by step also helped a lot.
Why is context important? The AI doesn't know my situation, so without context it guesses and gives generic answers.
Why review AI answers? AI can make mistakes, guess numbers and miss things, as it did with the priorities in Exercise C. I am still responsible for the final work.
How can AI help engineers across the SDLC? It can help draft plans, organise requirements, suggest designs, write and explain code, create tests, write deployment scripts and help fix problems later. The engineer always checks the results.
